L0287: Invalid trusted specification

The trusted declaration does not match a supported native operation or its specified signature. A trust boundary must name the actual operation, parameter passing and result shape. Correct the bridge; an unchecked arbitrary body is not a replacement for a verified implementation.

Example from `tests/corpus/reject/trusted_shape.lc`; the full file is a regression test.

```rust
trusted "same native item, incorrect runtime type"
fn wrong(xs: &Vec<u8>) -> (out: u8, @(out == 0)) = Vec::len;
```

Language, as built: [1.26:3](../../atlas.html#/doc/language/spec-1.26:3).
